/* Legacy theme for the generic confirm dialog -- reuses CCommonMessageBox's own native sprite art
   (the exact dialog family this primitive replaces), not a flat/programmatic panel. Composite is
   back-fill (stretched, painted first so it shows through the caps' transparent regions) + top cap
   + middle fill + bottom cap, mirroring CommonMessageBox.cpp's RenderFrame() paint order.

   Source pixel dimensions verified directly against each file's own header (OZT's TGA-style
   header at byte offset 16/18/20 for width/height/bit-depth; OZJ's wrapped JPEG SOF0 marker for
   width/height) -- not guessed. `newui_msgbox_top/middle/bottom.OZT` are exactly 230x67/230x15/
   230x50 at 32-bit, matching their own native draw constants (MSGBOX_TOP_HEIGHT/MIDDLE_HEIGHT/
   BOTTOM_HEIGHT) exactly. `newui_msgbox_back.OZJ` is actually 225x512 -- much taller than the
   panel ever needs, so it's authored to be CROPPED (top-left region, no stretch) rather than
   stretched-to-fit like the other three; the rect below (222x150) matches the back layer's own
   box size (`.gcd-sprite-back`'s 222x150 inset area) instead of the source's own full extent, to
   avoid vertically squashing a texture 3x taller than needed. */
@spritesheet msgbox-top-sheet
{
	src: "../../../newui_msgbox_top.tga";
	msgbox-top-image: 0px 0px 230px 67px;
}
@spritesheet msgbox-middle-sheet
{
	src: "../../../newui_msgbox_middle.tga";
	msgbox-middle-image: 0px 0px 230px 15px;
}
@spritesheet msgbox-bottom-sheet
{
	src: "../../../newui_msgbox_bottom.tga";
	msgbox-bottom-image: 0px 0px 230px 50px;
}
@spritesheet msgbox-back-sheet
{
	src: "../../../newui_msgbox_back.jpg";
	msgbox-back-image: 0px 0px 222px 150px;
}

/* #panel is centered via the .center-both utility class (generic_confirm_dialog.rml); every
   dimension is dp -- this is a LayoutMode::Dialog window (no transform:scale(root_scale)), same
   category as remember_password_prompt.rcss/msg_win.rcss, not the root_scale-tracking inventory-
   family windows -- so `dp`, not `-px`, is correct here (see base.rcss's header-rail-family
   comment for why that distinction matters). 230x160 matches native's own MSGBOX_WIDTH=230 and
   base 2-line height (67+50=117) plus room to grow -- see the fixed-panel simplification note in
   docs/rmlui-ui-system/dialog-migration-plan.md. No background-color/border here anymore -- the
   sprite composite below provides the frame, same as native. */
#panel {
	width: 230dp;
	height: 160dp;
	font-family: "Liberation Sans";
	font-size: 12dp;
	color: white;
}

.gcd-sprite-back {
	position: absolute;
	left: 4dp;
	right: 4dp;
	top: 5dp;
	bottom: 5dp;
	decorator: image(msgbox-back-image);
}
.gcd-sprite-top {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 0;
	height: 67dp;
	decorator: image(msgbox-top-image);
}
/* Stretches to fill the panel's remaining 160-67-50=43dp -- a single stretched fill rather than
   native's tiled repeat (native grows this by repeating a 15dp tile per extra wrapped line; this
   primitive uses a fixed-size panel instead, see the migration plan's own note on that tradeoff).
   Same "REPEAT fit mode isn't supported in this build" tradeoff base.rcss's own .panel-middle
   already documents. */
.gcd-sprite-middle {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 67dp;
	bottom: 50dp;
	decorator: image(msgbox-middle-image);
}
.gcd-sprite-bottom {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	height: 50dp;
	decorator: image(msgbox-bottom-image);
}

/* Text floats transparently over the sprite composite above, matching native (no separate boxed
   "well" -- CCommonMessageBox draws its text directly over its own composited background).
   left/right/top match native's own text metrics (MSGBOX_TEXT_TOP_BLANK=35,
   MSGBOX_TEXT_MAXWIDTH=180 out of the 230-wide panel = ~25dp side margin); bottom leaves a small
   gap above the buttons (repositioned below).

   top+bottom (not top+height) deliberately -- this engine's box model is content-box only (no
   box-sizing support anywhere in this codebase), so an explicit height combined with a bordered/
   padded box can push past the intended bottom edge (this bit us on the first pass of this file).
   Anchoring both edges keeps the box's outer size exactly (right - left) x (bottom - top)
   regardless of its own content. Content centers via flex (column direction, both axes) instead of
   top-aligning, so the message reads centered whether it's one short line or several. */
.gcd-body {
	position: absolute;
	left: 25dp;
	right: 25dp;
	top: 35dp;
	bottom: 56dp;
	overflow: auto hidden;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
}
.gcd-line {
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	text-align: center;
	white-space: normal;
	color: #ffe0a0;
}
.gcd-line.bold { font-weight: bold; }

/* top: 110dp = native's own vertical math for a fixed 160dp panel (160 - MSGBOX_BTN_BOTTOM_BLANK(20)
   - MSGBOX_BTN_HEIGHT(30)). Buttons stay the shared .btn sprite (op1_b_all.tga) with real bound
   text, not native's own baked OK/Cancel art -- this dialog's primary/secondary labels are
   data-driven (a future non-OK/Cancel-labeled dialog needs real text), and every current call site
   already uses the default OK/Cancel labels, so nothing is lost today either way. */
.btn.gcd-btn-primary, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary {
	top: 110dp;
	width: 54dp;
	height: 30dp;
}
.gcd-btn-primary   { left: 30dp; }
.gcd-btn-primary.solo { left: 88dp; }
.gcd-btn-secondary { left: 146dp; }
